@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam participantPadding 20
skinparam boxPadding 10

title Plum Claims Processing — Multi-Agent Orchestration (ReAct)

actor "Member" as MEMBER
actor "Ops Team" as OPS

box "Frontend" #E8F4FD
  participant "Streamlit UI" as UI
end box

box "Orchestrator Layer" #F0E6FF
  participant "Orchestrator Agent\n(LLM-powered)" as ORCH
  entity "Groq API\n(Llama3-70b)\n[Function Calling]" as GROQ_ORCH
end box

box "Tools (Agents)" #E8FFE8
  participant "extract_documents\n[Tool]" as EXT
  participant "validate_documents\n[Tool]" as VAL
  participant "deep_extract_documents\n[Tool]" as DEEP
  participant "evaluate_policy\n[Tool]" as POL
  participant "detect_fraud\n[Tool]" as FRAUD
  participant "decide_claim\n[Tool]" as DEC
end box

box "Infrastructure" #FFF3E0
  database "PostgreSQL" as DB
  entity "Groq API\n(Llama3)" as GROQ_EXT
end box

== 1. Claim Submission (SSE Stream) ==
MEMBER -> UI: Upload docs + fill form
UI -> ORCH: POST /api/claims [Accept: text/event-stream]
ORCH -> DB: INSERT claim (status=PROCESSING)
ORCH --> UI: SSE: { claim_id, status: PROCESSING }
note right #E8F4FD: SSE stream opened — live updates follow
UI --> MEMBER: "Processing claim..."

== 2. ReAct Loop: Orchestrator Decides Workflow ==
note right #F0E6FF
  Orchestrator receives claim info +
  system prompt with tool definitions.
  Calls Groq with function calling —
  LLM decides which tool(s) to call next.
  Each tool result feeds back as a
  "tool" message. Loop continues until
  decide_claim is called or error occurs.
end note

ORCH -> GROQ_ORCH: [system] tool definitions + workflow rules\n[user] claim details + "start processing"
GROQ_ORCH --> ORCH: tool_call: extract_documents({claim_id, documents})

== 3. Tool: extract_documents ==
ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "extraction", status: "running" }
ORCH -> EXT: extract_documents(claim_id, documents)
EXT -> GROQ_EXT: Classify doc type, assess quality, extract patient name
GROQ_EXT --> EXT: { doc_type, quality, patient_name, confidence }
EXT -> DB: INSERT Document records
EXT --> ORCH: { documents: [...], count: N, degraded: bool }

alt LLM fails
  EXT --> ORCH: degraded=true, fallback metadata
  note right #FFF3CD: Degraded mode — confidence drops
end

ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "extraction", status: "done", files: N }
ORCH -> GROQ_ORCH: tool_result: extraction complete\n→ LLM decides next step
GROQ_ORCH --> ORCH: tool_call: validate_documents({category, documents})

== 4. Tool: validate_documents (Early Exit) ==
ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "validation", status: "running" }
ORCH -> VAL: validate_documents(category, documents)
VAL -> VAL: Check types match category requirements
VAL -> VAL: Check quality scores
VAL -> VAL: Check patient name consistency

alt [Early Exit] Validation Fails
  VAL --> ORCH: { valid: false, errors: [...] }
  ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "validation", status: "failed", errors }
  ORCH --> UI: error event with specific actionable message
  UI --> MEMBER: Show error (e.g. "Expected HOSPITAL_BILL, got PRESCRIPTION")
  note right #FFB3B3: TC001 / TC002 / TC003 — stops here
else [Valid]
  VAL --> ORCH: { valid: true, errors: [] }
  ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "validation", status: "passed" }
  ORCH -> GROQ_ORCH: tool_result: validation passed
  GROQ_ORCH --> ORCH: tool_call: deep_extract_documents({claim_id, documents})
end

== 5. Tool: deep_extract_documents ==
ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "deep_extraction", status: "running" }
ORCH -> DEEP: deep_extract_documents(claim_id, validated_docs)
DEEP -> GROQ_EXT: Extract structured data (diagnosis, medicines, line items, etc.)
GROQ_EXT --> DEEP: structured JSON per document type

alt [Degraded] LLM timeout/parse failure
  DEEP --> ORCH: degraded=true, partial extraction
  note right #FFF3CD: TC011 — graceful degradation
  ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "deep_extraction", status: "degraded" }
else [Success]
  DEEP --> ORCH: full_extracted_data
  ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "deep_extraction", status: "done" }
end
DEEP -> DB: UPDATE Document (extracted_content, confidence)

ORCH -> GROQ_ORCH: tool_result: deep extraction complete
GROQ_ORCH --> ORCH: tool_call: evaluate_policy({...})  +  tool_call: detect_fraud({...})
note right #F0E6FF
  LLM can call multiple tools
  in parallel since policy and
  fraud are independent.
end note

== 6. Tool: evaluate_policy ==
ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "policy", status: "running" }
ORCH -> POL: evaluate_policy(member_id, category, amount, extracted_docs)
POL -> DB: LOAD policy_terms.json, member info
group Policy Checks
  POL -> POL: Coverage check
  POL -> POL: Waiting period check (TC005)
  POL -> POL: Exclusion check (TC012)
  POL -> POL: Pre-auth check (TC007)
  POL -> POL: Per-claim limit check (TC008)
  POL -> POL: Sub-limit check
  POL -> POL: Network discount calc (TC010)
  POL -> POL: Co-pay calc
end

alt Any check rejects
  POL --> ORCH: { eligible: false, rejection_reasons, checks }
  ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "policy", status: "rejected", reasons }
else All pass (possibly partial)
  POL --> ORCH: { eligible: true, approved_amount_estimate, checks }
  ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "policy", status: "passed" }
end
POL -> DB: INSERT PolicyCheck records

== 7. Tool: detect_fraud ==
ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "fraud", status: "running" }
ORCH -> FRAUD: detect_fraud(member_id, amount, treatment_date)
FRAUD -> DB: SELECT claims_history (same-day, same-month, high-value)
FRAUD -> FRAUD: Compare against fraud thresholds

alt Fraud score >= 0.8
  FRAUD --> ORCH: { fraud_score: 0.85, signals, flagged: true }
  note right #FFE0E0: TC009 — routed to manual review
  ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "fraud", status: "flagged", score: 0.85 }
else No signals
  FRAUD --> ORCH: { fraud_score: 0.0, signals: [], flagged: false }
  ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "fraud", status: "passed", score: 0.0 }
end
FRAUD -> DB: INSERT FraudCheck record

ORCH -> GROQ_ORCH: tool_results: policy + fraud complete
GROQ_ORCH --> ORCH: tool_call: decide_claim({all accumulated results})

== 8. Tool: decide_claim ==
ORCH --> UI: SSE: { step: "decision", status: "running" }
ORCH -> DEC: decide_claim(claim_id, validation, extraction, deep_extraction, policy, fraud)

note right #D4E6F1
  Decision Matrix:
  Validation failed? -> REJECTED
  Fraud >= 0.8?     -> MANUAL_REVIEW
  Policy rejected?  -> REJECTED
  Partial amount?   -> PARTIAL
  All clear?        -> APPROVED
  Degraded mode -> confidence penalty
end note

DEC --> ORCH: { decision, approved_amount, confidence, trace, breakdown }
DEC -> DB: INSERT DecisionRecord + full trace

ORCH -> DB: UPDATE Claim (status, decision, trace)
ORCH --> UI: SSE: { decision, approved_amount, trace, breakdown }
ORCH --> UI: SSE: [DONE]
UI --> MEMBER: Show result + expandable trace + live log

alt MANUAL_REVIEW
  UI --> OPS: Notify team for review
  OPS -> UI: Review trace, approve/override
end

== 9. Explainability (Always Available) ==
OPS -> ORCH: GET /api/claims/{id}/trace
ORCH -> DB: SELECT trace
ORCH --> OPS: Full step-by-step breakdown with all tool results

@enduml
